; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; USAGE NOTES FOR WEB BLAST
; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
;
; Option 1: QUICK VALIDATION (Recommended for case study)
;   - Submit ONLY forward primers (aroB_R1_F through group_306_R5_F)
;   - These are most critical for PCR specificity
;   - Saves time and focuses on off-target amplification risk
;
; Option 2: COMPREHENSIVE VALIDATION
;   - Submit this entire file (all 44 oligos)
;   - Forward primers determine amplicon specificity
;   - Reverse primers ensure amplicon termination
;   - Probes provide additional specificity layer (especially for off-target discrimination)
;
; BLAST PARAMETERS:
;   Database:           NCBI core_nt
;   Algorithm:          Blastn (somewhat similar sequences)
;   Word size:          7 (optimized for short oligos)
;   Expect threshold:   0.001 (stringent)
;   Short queries:      Checked (auto-adjust parameters)
;
; CRITICAL CHECKS:
;   ✓ C. muridarum matches:     NONE expected
;   ✓ C. suis matches:          NONE expected
;   ✓ C. trachomatis matches:   Expected (confirmatory)
;   ⚠️ Human DNA matches:        Evaluate separately (document if found)
;   ⚠️ Off-target bacteria:      None expected for exclusive targets
;
; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
